{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been feeling really sick since yesterday evening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been vomiting nonstop—more than ten times—and I’ve had diarrhea too. I also had a fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any belly pain or blood in the vomit or stool?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no blood and not much pain. But I feel weak and dizzy when I stand up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your blood pressure drops when you stand, which we call orthostasis. It’s likely from losing fluids due to vomiting and diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. My son was sick first—he had diarrhea yesterday. My husband started feeling off tonight too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That helps explain it. It sounds like a stomach virus going around your household. Given your transplant history, we’re being extra careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, because I’m on immunosuppressants. Should I stop any of my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you should keep taking your transplant meds—Cellcept, sirolimus, prednisone—as usual. Stopping them could risk rejection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. My blood sugars have been all over the place—from 80 to over 300."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common when you’re sick and not eating regularly. We’re monitoring your glucose and keeping your insulin pump on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I can keep the pump. It helps me stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep it running. We’ve started IV fluids to help with dehydration and to keep your kidneys protected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I already feel a little better since the Zofran kicked in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll keep an eye on your nausea. We also did a chest X-ray to rule out pneumonia, and it looked clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-06-04 00:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had any cough or shortness of breath, so that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-06-04 01:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested for flu—both A and B—and it came back negative. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-06-04 01:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not the flu. Could it be something else, like CMV?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-06-04 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s why we ordered a CMV viral load. Given your transplant, CMV is a concern, but your initial blood test didn’t detect it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-06-04 01:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So that’s probably not it either?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-06-04 01:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this point. The most likely cause is a viral gastroenteritis, especially with your family getting sick too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning show your kidney function is stable. Creatinine is 0.9, which is normal for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. What about the urine test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of infection—no nitrites, blood, or white cells. The mixed flora likely means contamination, not a UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I wasn’t surprised—my catheter was tricky to place last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We also checked your stool—no Salmonella, Shigella, Campylobacter, or C. diff. All negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s definitely not food poisoning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-06-04 06:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. Everything points to a viral cause. You’re already improving—less nausea, tolerating sips."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-06-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat labs show your white count went up a bit, but that’s expected with infection. No signs of sepsis—lactate is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-06-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure? I still feel a little lightheaded."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-06-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your BP is improving—105/44 lying down, and you’re not symptomatic. We’ll keep giving fluids and hold your atenolol for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-06-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I should skip my blood pressure pill?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-06-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just temporarily. Once you’re eating and your BP stabilizes, we’ll restart it at a lower dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Afebrile, no vomiting in over 12 hours, and you kept down toast and applesauce."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you this morning. We’ll send you home with some oral Zofran in case nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my meds? Anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most are the same. We’re adjusting your atenolol to half a 25mg tablet daily. Sirolimus is now 2mg daily—two 1mg tablets."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to update my pill organizer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Drink plenty of fluids and stick to the BRAT diet for a few days. Follow up with your transplant team about the CMV and culture results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-06-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest, and call if you develop fever, severe pain, or can’t keep fluids down."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-06-04 00:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-06-05 19:19:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of two kidney transplants was admitted for acute nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea lasting one day, accompanied by low-grade fever and orthostatic hypotension. She reported sick contacts—her young son and husband—developing similar symptoms. Initial evaluation revealed volume depletion, but no signs of bacterial infection, C. difficile, or influenza. CMV viral load was not detected. She was managed with IV fluids, continued immunosuppressive therapy, and symptom control with Zofran. Her condition improved rapidly, with resolution of vomiting and fever, and she began tolerating oral intake. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue all baseline medications, adjusted atenolol dose, and follow up on pending culture and viral load results.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Insulin pump status",
      "Malignant neoplasm of breast (female), unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Diabetes with peripheral circulatory disorders, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Peripheral angiopathy in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Volume depletion, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
